{"book":16,"chapter":10,"rubric":"FROM ASSEMBLER TO C / PROJECTS AND TOOLING / CHAPTER 10","slides":[{"title":"Translation units","sub":"Chapter 10 · from .c to a program","short":"Stages","main":"Each .c is its own object file; the linker joins them.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Translation unit","Pipeline","Linker"],"captions":["Each .c is a translation unit: preprocessor, compiler, assembler turn it into an object file","gcc -E, -S, -c stop after that stage; an object file is machine code plus a symbol table","The linker joins object files into a program, the last step you saw in the assembler book"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":60.0,"y":60.0,"w":80.0,"h":28.0,"text":"main.c","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":60.0,"y":100.0,"w":80.0,"h":28.0,"text":"util.c","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":180.0,"y":60.0,"w":80.0,"h":28.0,"text":"main.o","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"d","x":180.0,"y":100.0,"w":80.0,"h":28.0,"text":"util.o","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":102.0,"y1":60.0,"x2":138.0,"y2":60.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":102.0,"y1":100.0,"x2":138.0,"y2":100.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":40.0,"y":76.0,"w":50.0,"h":26.0,"text":".c","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":110.0,"y":76.0,"w":50.0,"h":26.0,"text":".i","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":180.0,"y":76.0,"w":50.0,"h":26.0,"text":".s","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"d","x":250.0,"y":76.0,"w":50.0,"h":26.0,"text":".o","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"e","x":320.0,"y":76.0,"w":50.0,"h":26.0,"text":"exe","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":66.0,"y1":76.0,"x2":86.0,"y2":76.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":136.0,"y1":76.0,"x2":156.0,"y2":76.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e3","x1":206.0,"y1":76.0,"x2":226.0,"y2":76.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e4","x1":276.0,"y1":76.0,"x2":296.0,"y2":76.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":120.0,"text":"-E        -S        -c","size":9.0,"mono":true}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":60.0,"y":50.0,"w":80.0,"h":26.0,"text":"main.o","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":60.0,"y":90.0,"w":80.0,"h":26.0,"text":"util.o","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":200.0,"y":70.0,"w":100.0,"h":40.0,"text":"linker","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"d","x":320.0,"y":70.0,"w":70.0,"h":26.0,"text":"app","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":102.0,"y1":50.0,"x2":150.0,"y2":62.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":102.0,"y1":90.0,"x2":150.0,"y2":78.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e3","x1":252.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":284.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6}]],"cues":[15.3,31.1]}]},{"title":"Declaration and definition","sub":"One definition","short":"Definition","main":"Multiple definition and undefined reference are link errors.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Declaration","Definition","Two errors"],"captions":["A declaration says a name exists and its type: extern int x; int f(void); you may have many","A definition creates the thing, memory or code; there is exactly one per program","Two definitions: \"multiple definition\"; none: \"undefined reference\"; both happen at link time"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["extern int counter;","int add(int a, int b);"],"lang":"c","size":11.0,"lh":26.0,"w":320.0},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":120.0,"text":"in a header: what exists","size":9.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["int counter = 0;","int add(int a, int b) {","    return a + b;","}"],"hl":[0,1],"lang":"c","size":11.0,"lh":22.0,"w":320.0},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":130.0,"text":"in one .c: the thing itself","size":9.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["multiple definition of `counter'","undefined reference to `add'"],"bad":[0,1],"lang":"c","size":10.5,"lh":28.0,"w":345.0}]],"cues":[11.8,23.5]}]},{"title":"static and linkage","sub":"Internal names","short":"static","main":"File-level static hides a name; in a function it keeps state.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["External by default","static hides the name","static inside a function"],"captions":["Functions and globals are visible to the whole program by default: external linkage","File-level static makes a name internal: not in the symbol table, no clashes with others","static inside a function is different: created once, remembers its value between calls"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":100.0,"h":28.0,"text":"a.c: int f()","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":250.0,"y":60.0,"w":100.0,"h":28.0,"text":"b.c: call f()","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":200.0,"y1":60.0,"x2":190.0,"y2":60.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":110.0,"text":"f visible from b.c","size":9.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["static int helper(int x) { … }","static int calls;   // only in this file"],"hl":[0,1],"lang":"c","size":10.0,"lh":26.0,"w":330.0},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":120.0,"text":"not part of the module interface","size":9.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["int next_id(void) {","    static int id = 0;","    return ++id;     // 1, 2, 3, …","}"],"hl":[1],"lang":"c","size":10.5,"lh":22.0,"w":320.0}]],"cues":[9.0,27.2]}]},{"title":"Header as interface","sub":"Opaque types","short":"Header","main":"The .h holds declarations; the type's layout hides in .c.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["What goes in a header","Opaque type","Hidden implementation"],"captions":["Headers hold prototypes, types, constants, macros; the implementation and helpers stay in .c","Opaque type: the header has only struct stack; and prototypes taking a pointer to it","The full struct is in .c: users can't see fields, and you can change it without rebuilding clients"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"h","x":90.0,"y":76.0,"w":110.0,"h":34.0,"text":"stack.h\ninterface","tone":"yellow","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":250.0,"y":76.0,"w":110.0,"h":34.0,"text":"stack.c\nimplementation","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":200.0,"y1":76.0,"x2":190.0,"y2":76.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6}],[{"t":"code","id":"c~code","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["/* stack.h */","struct stack;","struct stack *stack_new(void);","void stack_push(struct stack *, int);"],"hl":[1],"lang":"c","size":10.0,"lh":22.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c~code","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["/* stack.c */","struct stack { int *a; size_t n, cap; };","struct stack *stack_new(void) { … }"],"hl":[1],"lang":"c","size":9.5,"lh":24.0,"w":330.0}]],"cues":[13.3,27.6]}]},{"title":"Symbol table","sub":"nm and prefixes","short":"Symbols","main":"Names are not mangled: use prefixes.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["nm","Name clash","Prefixes"],"captions":["An object file keeps a symbol table: what it defines (T, D, B) and refers to (U); inspect with nm","C does not mangle names: two modules with a function init clash","Prefix a module's public names: list_init; names starting with _ and a capital, or __, are reserved"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["$ nm util.o","0000 T add","0000 D counter","     U printf"],"hl":[1,2],"lang":"c","size":10.5,"lh":22.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":70.0,"w":100.0,"h":28.0,"text":"a.c: init()","tone":"red","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":250.0,"y":70.0,"w":100.0,"h":28.0,"text":"b.c: init()","tone":"red","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":120.0,"text":"multiple definition of `init'","tone":"red","size":9.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["list_init, list_push, list_free","_Reserved  __internal   // ✕ reserved"],"hl":[0],"bad":[1],"lang":"c","size":10.0,"lh":28.0,"w":330.0}]],"cues":[12.8,34.0]}]},{"title":"Linker","sub":"Sections and relocations","short":"Relocations","main":"S + A for absolute addresses, S + A − P for relative ones.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Sections","Addresses","Relocation"],"captions":["Same-named sections of all objects are merged: code in .text, data in .data, zeros in .bss","The linker assigns them addresses with alignment; every symbol gets a real address","A relocation is \"offset, symbol, type, addend\": absolute = S + A, relative = S + A − P"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"t","x":70.0,"y":50.0,"w":100.0,"h":26.0,"text":".text a + b","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"d","x":70.0,"y":90.0,"w":100.0,"h":26.0,"text":".data a + b","tone":"yellow","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"s","x":70.0,"y":130.0,"w":100.0,"h":26.0,"text":".bss a + b","tone":"muted","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":270.0,"y":90.0,"text":"sections\nmerged","size":9.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["0x10000  .text","0x10200  .data","0x10240  .bss","0x10300  main  ← symbol"],"hl":[3],"lang":"c","size":10.5,"lh":22.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"a","x":20.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["call f        # address of f unknown","// reloc: offset=0 sym=f type=PC32"],"lang":"asm","size":9.5,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":124.0,"text":"S + A − P → into the instruction field","tone":"green","size":10.0,"mono":true}]],"cues":[13.7,27.6]}]},{"title":"Static libraries","sub":"ar and order","short":"Static","main":"Libraries go after the files that refer to them.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["ar and .a","Only what's needed","Order matters"],"captions":["ar packs object files into an .a archive, a static library","The linker pulls from the archive only the objects needed for undefined symbols","The archive is scanned once, left to right: list libraries AFTER the objects using them; cycles: a group"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["$ ar rcs libutil.a a.o b.o c.o","$ gcc main.o -L. -lutil -o app"],"hl":[0],"lang":"c","size":10.0,"lh":26.0,"w":330.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"l","x":80.0,"y":76.0,"w":120.0,"h":70.0,"text":"libutil.a\na.o  b.o  c.o","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"m","x":250.0,"y":50.0,"w":90.0,"h":26.0,"text":"main.o: U b","tone":"yellow","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"p","x":250.0,"y":100.0,"w":90.0,"h":26.0,"text":"take b.o","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":200.0,"y1":76.0,"x2":206.0,"y2":98.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["gcc -lutil main.o      // ✕ not found","gcc main.o -lutil      // ✓","gcc main.o -Wl,--start-group -la -lb -Wl,--end-group"],"hl":[1,2],"bad":[0],"lang":"c","size":9.0,"lh":24.0,"w":345.0}]],"cues":[13.9,28.2]}]},{"title":"Dynamic libraries","sub":"-fPIC and binding time","short":"Dynamic","main":"Static binds at build time, dynamic at run time.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Not copied","-fPIC","When we bind"],"captions":["A dynamic library (.so) is not copied into the program: the linker only notes the needed symbols","Code is made position independent: -fPIC; smaller size and updates without rebuild, but version dependency","The difference is binding time: static at build, dynamic at run time (details in the Unix book)"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":80.0,"y":60.0,"w":100.0,"h":30.0,"text":"app","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":250.0,"y":60.0,"w":110.0,"h":30.0,"text":"libm.so","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":130.0,"y1":60.0,"x2":192.0,"y2":60.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":110.0,"text":"a reference, not a copy","size":9.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["$ gcc -fPIC -shared util.c -o libutil.so","$ gcc main.c -L. -lutil -o app"],"hl":[0],"lang":"c","size":9.5,"lh":26.0,"w":330.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":50.0,"w":120.0,"h":28.0,"text":"static: at build","tone":"yellow","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":90.0,"y":100.0,"w":120.0,"h":28.0,"text":"dynamic: at run","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":280.0,"y":76.0,"text":"binding\ntime","size":9.5}]],"cues":[13.6,29.9]}]},{"title":"make: rules","sub":"Dependency graph","short":"make","main":"A target is stale if missing or older than a dependency.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Rule","Dependency graph","Rebuild"],"captions":["A rule: target, colon, dependencies; below, commands, each line starting with a tab","make builds a dependency graph: app depends on main.o and util.o, which depend on their .c","A target is rebuilt if missing or older than any dependency; editing util.c rebuilds only util.o and app"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["app: main.o util.o","<TAB>gcc main.o util.o -o app","","main.o: main.c","<TAB>gcc -c main.c"],"hl":[0,3],"lang":"c","size":10.0,"lh":20.0,"w":345.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":180.0,"y":30.0,"w":80.0,"h":26.0,"text":"app","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":110.0,"y":80.0,"w":80.0,"h":26.0,"text":"main.o","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c~cell","x":250.0,"y":80.0,"w":80.0,"h":26.0,"text":"util.o","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"d","x":110.0,"y":130.0,"w":80.0,"h":24.0,"text":"main.c","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"e","x":250.0,"y":130.0,"w":80.0,"h":24.0,"text":"util.c","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":155.0,"y1":43.0,"x2":125.0,"y2":67.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":205.0,"y1":43.0,"x2":235.0,"y2":67.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e3","x1":110.0,"y1":93.0,"x2":110.0,"y2":118.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e4","x1":250.0,"y1":93.0,"x2":250.0,"y2":118.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":180.0,"y":30.0,"w":80.0,"h":26.0,"text":"app","tone":"red","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":110.0,"y":80.0,"w":80.0,"h":26.0,"text":"main.o","tone":"muted","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c~cell","x":250.0,"y":80.0,"w":80.0,"h":26.0,"text":"util.o","tone":"red","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"d","x":110.0,"y":130.0,"w":80.0,"h":24.0,"text":"main.c","tone":"muted","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"e","x":250.0,"y":130.0,"w":80.0,"h":24.0,"text":"util.c","tone":"yellow","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":155.0,"y1":43.0,"x2":125.0,"y2":67.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":205.0,"y1":43.0,"x2":235.0,"y2":67.0,"tone":"red","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e3","x1":110.0,"y1":93.0,"x2":110.0,"y2":118.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e4","x1":250.0,"y1":93.0,"x2":250.0,"y2":118.0,"tone":"red","arrow":true,"width":1.6}]],"cues":[12.1,31.1]}]},{"title":"Variables and patterns","sub":"%.o: %.c","short":"Patterns","main":"$@, $<, $^ and .PHONY.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Variables","Pattern rule","Automatic"],"captions":["CC and CFLAGS set the compiler and flags: $(CC) $(CFLAGS) …; change a value in one place","%.o: %.c says how to get a .o from any .c, one rule instead of ten","$@ is the target, $< the first dependency, $^ all of them; fake targets (clean) go in .PHONY"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["CC = gcc","CFLAGS = -Wall -Wextra -O2","app: $(OBJ)","\t$(CC) $^ -o $@"],"hl":[0,1],"lang":"c","size":10.0,"lh":22.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["%.o: %.c","\t$(CC) $(CFLAGS) -c $< -o $@"],"hl":[0],"lang":"c","size":11.0,"lh":28.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["$@   target","$<   first dependency","$^   all dependencies",".PHONY: clean"],"hl":[3],"lang":"c","size":10.5,"lh":22.0,"w":320.0}]],"cues":[10.8,29.4]}]},{"title":"Header dependencies","sub":"-MMD -MP","short":"-MMD","main":".d files keep the graph honest.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Weak spot","-MMD -MP","include"],"captions":["make knows only listed dependencies: editing a header missing from the rule rebuilds nothing","The compiler with -MMD -MP writes a .d file next to each .o listing the included headers","The Makefile pulls them in with -include: the graph always matches the real #include lines"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"h","x":90.0,"y":50.0,"w":80.0,"h":26.0,"text":"util.h","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":90.0,"y":100.0,"w":80.0,"h":26.0,"text":"main.c","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"o","x":250.0,"y":100.0,"w":80.0,"h":26.0,"text":"main.o","tone":"red","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":130.0,"y1":100.0,"x2":206.0,"y2":100.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":270.0,"y":50.0,"text":"util.h edit\nunseen by make","tone":"red","size":9.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c~code","x":10.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["main.o: main.c util.h config.h","util.h:","config.h:   # -MP: dummy targets"],"hl":[0],"lang":"c","size":9.5,"lh":24.0,"w":345.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c~code","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["CFLAGS += -MMD -MP","-include $(OBJ:.o=.d)"],"hl":[0,1],"lang":"c","size":11.0,"lh":28.0,"w":320.0}]],"cues":[19.3,20.3]}]},{"title":"Project layout","sub":"Directories and flags","short":"Layout","main":"Public and internal headers; -Wall -Wextra.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Directories","Public vs internal","Warnings"],"captions":["src for sources, include for public headers, tests for tests, build for output you can delete whole","A public header has only what clients need; the internal one sits next to the sources","Always -Wall -Wextra, optimize for release; big projects use CMake, a generator of the same graphs"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["project/","  src/      include/","  tests/    build/","  Makefile"],"lang":"c","size":11.0,"lh":24.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":120.0,"h":28.0,"text":"include/util.h","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":90.0,"y":104.0,"w":120.0,"h":28.0,"text":"src/util_impl.h","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":280.0,"y":60.0,"text":"for clients","size":9.5},{"t":"text","id":"m","x":280.0,"y":104.0,"text":"own only","size":9.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["CFLAGS = -Wall -Wextra -g","release: CFLAGS += -O2 -DNDEBUG"],"hl":[0,1],"lang":"c","size":10.0,"lh":28.0,"w":330.0}]],"cues":[13.1,27.7]}]},{"title":"Summary","sub":"What's next","short":"Summary","main":"Next: undefined behavior and sanitizers.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Files and names","Libraries and make","Next"],"captions":["Each .c compiles separately; one definition, many declarations; static hides names, headers are interfaces, opaque types hide layout","Relocations fix addresses; static libraries go after their users; make rebuilds by graph; -MMD keeps it honest","Next: undefined behavior, debugging, and sanitizers"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":110.0,"h":28.0,"text":"1 definition","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":250.0,"y":60.0,"w":110.0,"h":28.0,"text":"static and .h","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":116.0,"text":"module = interface + implementation","tone":"green","size":9.5}],[{"t":"cell",